# Cursor Rules for First-Principles Transformer

## Code Style
- Use professional, functional, intelligent, modular, concise, elegant code
- Clear comments explaining the "why" not just the "what"
- Documentation should be understated and "show not tell"
- Follow Python PEP 8 style guidelines

## Development Approach
- Test-driven development (TDD) with unified modular approach
- All modules should have corresponding tests
- Use real data analysis, no mock methods
- Modular, well-documented, clearly reasoned code

## File Organization
- Keep modules focused and single-purpose
- Separate concerns: components, visualization, utilities
- Clear import structure and dependencies

## Transformer-Specific
- Always track both information highways:
  - Residual stream (vertical flow through layers)
  - K/V stream (horizontal flow across positions)
- Enable state tracking for visualization and analysis
- Maintain clear separation between computation and visualization

## Testing
- Comprehensive test coverage for all components
- Test both individual components and integration
- Include tests for visualization functions
- Test edge cases and error conditions

## Documentation
- Clear docstrings for all public functions and classes
- Explain the conceptual purpose, not just mechanics
- Reference the information flow architecture in comments
- Include usage examples where helpful

## Visualization
- All visualizations should be clear and informative
- Support both static and animated outputs
- Enable customization of visualization parameters
- Save outputs with descriptive names


